    "q-84312": {
      "dom_id": "step-q84312",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Two biased coins are tossed several times. The results are recorded below. Based on this data, if the random variable $X$ represents the number of heads obtained on a random toss, what is $\\text{SD}[X]?$\n\n| Number of heads | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Frequency | $4$ | $12$ | $9$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The standard deviation of a random variable $X$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]},\n$$\n\nwhere the variance can be computed using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute the probability mass function $f(x).$ To do this, we divide each frequency by the total, which is $4+12+9=25.$ We get the following result:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{4}{25}$ | $\\frac{12}{25}$ | $\\frac{9}{25}$ |\n\nNow, we compute $\\text{E}[X]$ by summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{4}{25})+1(\\frac{12}{25})+2(\\frac{9}{25}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{4}{25})+1(\\frac{12}{25})+4(\\frac{9}{25}) \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{25}-{(\\frac{6}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{25}-\\frac{36}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{12}{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
