    "q-129041": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129041",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "If $\\text{E}[X]=3.5$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=18,$ then what is $\\text{Var}[X]?$",
      "worked_solution": "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =18-{3.5}^{2} \\\\  & =18-12.25 \\\\  & =5.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
