    "q-129110": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129110",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Two fair  four-sided dice are rolled and $X$ is the absolute difference of their scores. The probability mass function $f(x)$ of $X$ is shown in the table below. What is $\\text{SD}[X]?$ \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The standard deviation of a random variable $X$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]},\n$$\n\nwhere the variance can be computed using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{4})+1(\\frac{3}{8})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{4})+1(\\frac{3}{8})+4(\\frac{1}{4})+9(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-{(\\frac{5}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{25}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{15}{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
