    "q-129376": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129376",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Let $X$ be the number obtained by a spinner with five sections labeled $-2,-1,0,1,2.$ The probability mass function $f(x)$ of $X$ is shown in the table below. What is $\\text{Var}[X]?$\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ |",
      "worked_solution": "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =(-2)\\cdot f(-2)+(-1)\\cdot f(-1)+0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2) \\\\  & =(-2)(\\frac{1}{8})+(-1)(\\frac{1}{4})+0(\\frac{3}{8})+1(\\frac{1}{16})+2(\\frac{3}{16}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & =(-2)^{2}\\cdot f(-2)+(-1)^{2}\\cdot f(-1)+{0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{8})+1(\\frac{1}{4})+0(\\frac{3}{8})+1(\\frac{1}{16})+4(\\frac{3}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{16}-{(-\\frac{1}{16})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{16}-\\frac{1}{256} \\\\  & =\\frac{400}{256}-\\frac{1}{256} \\\\  & =\\frac{399}{256}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
